Umm, I have, but I'd have to muck around with my machine to check 
the details (sketch follows). I'm 99% sure I've managed to get it 
working with the current downloadable binary, but it was months 
ago. :-)

[Something about my built-from-source dual TTY/Qt of 3.4.3 is a bit 
broken as far as OS X is concerned, and doesn't allow this to work. 
Note to DevTeam Mac guys, that was a gentle hint]

Essentially: You have to launch the GUI app from the terminal (or a 
script that sends 'do shell script', or ...). But that may well 
fail due to a chdir not working. To get around that you need to 
create symlinks (not aliases!!) in the same parent directory as the 
target of the terminal (or script...) command to the nethack 
directory.

You'll need to create a user named "wizard" (as that's the name 
compiled in by default, aiui). I simply logged in as that user, but 
I guess you should be able to su to it instead <shrug> I don't play 
in Debug or eXplore mode, so I've only done this a few times as 
'how would I?' experiments.

The command for terminal (assuming a 'normal' Mac OS X install 
location) ends up being something like:

/Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents/MacOS/nethack -D 
-u"Lintilla234"


The nethackdir (that the nethack targeted above needs to access is 
at /Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/nethackdir)


As you might guess, the process for starting in eXplore mode (to 
get the wand) is much the same, except the switch is -X instead of 
-D

